# HDC automation

- Prefer the **hdc** CLI from the hdc repo root (`hdc.cmd` on Windows, `./hdc` on Unix after chmod). Do not tell operators to run `hdc` in docs, examples, or chat. Do not invent hostnames, IPs, or credentials.
- **This repo (hdc-clumps):** Package code under `{clients,infrastructure,services}/<id>/`. Bootstrap cache: `hdc clumps init` (from hdc repo root). Package scripts import shared runtime via `hdc/package/*` (`../hdc/apps/hdc-cli/lib/package/`).
- **Static IP planning:** Read `hdc-private/operations/ip-allocations.md` for IP group boundaries and next-free addresses; cross-check `services/bind/config.json` (in hdc-private) and `operations/inventory/systems/*.json` before assigning. Do not store literal site IPs in public repos.
- **Greenfield service deploy:** Follow `.cursor/skills/hdc-service-deploy/SKILL.md` — ask discovery questions, write `plan.md` in hdc-private, get approval, then deploy and fix scripts; optional bind/nginx-waf/cloudflare only with user consent.
- **Private operator data:** Clump `config.json`, clump `.env`, and `operations/inventory` / `operations/automated` JSON live in the sibling **hdc-private** repo (or `HDC_PRIVATE_ROOT` in hdc root `.env`) with the same relative paths as packages here (`services/<id>/config.json`, etc.). Resolution: hdc-clumps example first, then hdc-private merge for config and `.env`. Global hdc root `.env` holds vault/secret-backend only; clump `.env` loads on `hdc run` / daily maintain for that package.
- Structured facts live in `operations/inventory/{systems,networks,services,targets}/` as `*.json` in **hdc-private** (`kind`: `system`, `network`, `target`, or `services`). **System** records may list **`services`**: `{ "id": "<id>", "nodes"?: ["…"] }` pointing at **`kind: "services"`** sidecars under `operations/inventory/services/` (by `id` only). Schemas under `../hdc/apps/hdc-cli/schema/inventory.*.schema.json`. Auth fields reference **env var names** only, never secret values.
- **System ids:** follow `.cursor/rules/hdc-inventory-naming.mdc` — class prefix (`vm-`, *(none)*, …) for non-physical systems; physical hosts unprefixed; instance letters (`-a`, `-b`) not numbers.
- Never commit or paste `.env` contents or live `config.json` in this repo.
- **Packages** (plugins) live under `{infrastructure,services,clients}/<id>/manifest.json` with `deploy/`, `maintain/`, and `query/` scripts (`run.mjs`). **Home clients:** `clients/{windows,ubuntu,raspberrypi}/` each with its own `config.json` in hdc-private (`hdc run client windows maintain`, `hdc run client client-ubuntu query`, …). Orchestration stays in Node.
- **Logging:** For `hdc run <tier> <clump> … query|deploy`, log user-visible progress on **stderr** only; keep **stdout** clean for JSON when the CLI parses it. See `.cursor/rules/hdc-automation-logging.mdc` (required checks for package `*.mjs` changes).
- **QEMU guest agent:** For Proxmox **QEMU** deploy paths (not LXC), enable `agent=1` after clone and install `qemu-guest-agent` in the guest when SSH is available. See [`.cursor/rules/proxmox-qemu-guest-agent.mdc`](proxmox-qemu-guest-agent.mdc).
- **Guest maintain baseline:** Service `maintain` on Linux Proxmox guests ensures the `hdc` automation user, local sudo admin, ClamAV, `unattended-upgrades`, CrowdSec/Wazuh agents (from `infrastructure/proxmox/config.json` `provision.guest_agents` in hdc-private), mail relay, and disables root SSH when both users succeed. Shared helpers: `hdc/package/guest-linux-baseline.mjs`, `hdc/package/guest-ssh-resolve.mjs`, `hdc/package/guest-ssh-exec.mjs`.
- **Masked secrets:** Vault passphrases, `hdc secrets set` values, and `getSecret()` prompts use **`readLineQuestion(q, { mask: true })`** via `../hdc/apps/hdc-cli/lib/readline-masked.mjs`. Non-TTY falls back to visible input with a warning.
- **Selective maintain filters:** Flags like `--site` (nginx / nginx-waf), `--rule` (unifi-network), or `--zone` (cloudflare) must not implicitly delete unrelated live resources. Use explicit `--prune` (or full maintain without a site filter) when removal is intended.
- **No root scratch scripts (`tmp-*`):** Never create `tmp-*` at the **repo root** of hdc-clumps or hdc-private. Prefer `hdc run …` and existing clump flags first. When a one-off helper is unavoidable in hdc, put it only under `../hdc/tools/scripts/tmp-<short-purpose>.mjs` — gitignored. Prefer extending hdc-clumps packages over new tools scripts.
- **Agent knowledge (OKF):** Start recall at `../hdc-private/ai-docs/index.md` (only OKF bundle). After a durable package learning, promote there per `.cursor/rules/hdc-okf-ai-docs.mdc` and skill `hdc-okf`; human prose stays under `../hdc/docs/`.
